# The harness dragging a slider — the thing it could not do until now.
#
# `Action::Click` is a press and a release delivered inside one frozen frame, so
# the demo never runs an update with the button down and `Response::held` is
# never true. Every drag widget in the toolkit acts on `held` and nothing else
# (see `slmsttaa-ui/src/widgets/slider.rs`), so a click on a slider track did
# exactly nothing — which meant the transport's rate, both erosion `log_slider`s
# and every numeric knob in every demo were unreachable by a capture script.
# `capture/terrain-plot.script` still records the workaround it had to use: it
# advanced the bake by *playing* to the pass it wanted, because it could not
# scrub to one.
#
# `press` and `release` are separate steps, so the button stays down across
# checkpoints and real frames run in between. This file is the check.
#
# Run it:  cargo xtask shoot terrain --script capture/terrain-drag.script
#
# Coordinates are physical pixels from the window's top-left, read off `shot
# rest` at the default 1280x800. The `passes/sec` track spans x 22..331 at
# y 190, and the panel does not reflow under any step here: the Bake section
# draws every row unconditionally, and pausing only swaps a button's label.

# Frame 200: about pass 26, still baking, `passes/sec` at its default 8 with the
# knob a quarter of the way along. The reference shot.
200  shot  rest

# Pause, so the only thing that changes between the shots below is the slider.
# The move is on an earlier frame than the click on purpose — a frozen frame
# runs no update, so the demo has to be let run once with the pointer in its new
# place before anything is aimed there. Getting this wrong looks exactly like the
# click missing.
220  move  97 109
240  click
260  shot  paused

# The drag. Onto the knob first, and again with a gap before the press so hover
# is established by a real frame.
280  move  97 190
300  press

# Button still down. The cursor moves to the middle of the track and the knob
# has to come with it — this is the frame that could not exist before, and the
# shot is taken while the button is *still held*.
320  move  200 190
330  shot  midway

# On to the right-hand end, then let go.
340  move  300 190
360  release

# Frame 380: `passes/sec` reads 27 instead of 8, the knob is at the far end, and
# the pass counter has not moved because the demo is paused. A click at the same
# coordinates leaves this picture identical to `paused`, which is the negative
# result this file exists to distinguish itself from.
380  shot  dragged
